              {
                "text": "**Analyzing the Patterns**\n\nI'm currently focused on identifying patterns within the training examples. Specifically, I'm analyzing the relationship between the input data (rectangles of numbers and scattered digits) and the corresponding output pixels. I'm noting the pixel counts. I've observed that the presence of 7s seems significant in generating output pixels. I'm trying to quantify how the output pixels relate to the positions and number of input data values.\n\n\n**Projecting Digit Positions**\n\nOkay, I've got a handle on how the 7s are being placed. It seems like the input 7s project to the nearest points on the border surrounding the rectangle of digits. I'm seeing this with different rectangles, specifically how the input data influences the color 7 pixels. I need to verify this projection rule with more examples, especially with the 6-box in Example 2. Let's see how those 7s get mapped!\n\n\n**Verifying Coordinate Clamping**\n\nOkay, I'm now testing a coordinate clamping approach. It looks like each input \"1\" is mapped to a position on the border surrounding its digit box. The idea is to take the coordinates of each input digit and *clamp* them to the surrounding ring. For the \"1s\" in Example 2, this clamping seems to be working, I'm going to look at other examples.\n\n\n",
                "type": "reasoning_text"
              }
            ],
