                "annotations": [],
                "text": "Answering the task with the following transformation rule:\n1. Identify the solid rectangular block of color C1 and find its bounding box `[r_min, r_max] x [c_min, c_max]`.\n2. The target border is the 1-pixel expansion of this block: `[r_min - 1, r_max + 1] x [c_min - 1, c_max + 1]`.\n3. For every scattered pixel of the other color C2, project (clamp) its row and column coordinates to this expanded bounding box: `r' = clamp(r, r_min - 1, r_max + 1)` and `c' = clamp(c, c_min - 1, c_max + 1)`.\n4. In the output grid, keep the rectangular block intact, place the projected C2 pixels at their new clamped coordinates, and set all other cells to 0.",
